{
  "description": "Group mailbox key schedule vectors (docs/design/group-mailboxes.md in haskou/pigeon-swarm-node, section Derivation). Generated with node:crypto hkdfSync, independent of the UI implementation.",
  "algorithms": {
    "hkdf": "HKDF-SHA256 (RFC 5869), empty salt, 32-byte output.",
    "slot": "base64url(HKDF(ikm = generationSecret, info = utf8(labels.slot) || utf8(identityId))), unpadded. Decision (a) of haskou/pigeon-swarm-ui#174: the slot is derived, not random, because gen_k is member-only.",
    "mailboxId": "base64url(HKDF(ikm = generationSecret, info = utf8(labels.mailboxId) || slot)), unpadded; slot is the 32 raw bytes.",
    "postToken": "base64url(HKDF(ikm = generationSecret, info = utf8(labels.postToken) || slot)), unpadded.",
    "envelopeKey": "hex(HKDF(ikm = generationSecret, info = utf8(labels.envelopeKey) || slot)); the AES-256-GCM key of the per-copy outer AEAD (D5).",
    "readToken": "base64url(HKDF(ikm = ownerRootKey, info = utf8(labels.readToken) || utf8(mailboxId))), unpadded; the same derivation as the one-to-one read token."
  },
  "labels": {
    "slot": "pigeon/group-mailbox/slot/v1",
    "mailboxId": "pigeon/group-mailbox/id/v1",
    "postToken": "pigeon/group-mailbox/post/v1",
    "envelopeKey": "pigeon/group-mailbox/envelope/v1",
    "readToken": "pigeon/mailbox/read/v1"
  },
  "inputEncoding": "generationSecret (gen_k) and ownerRootKey (rootKey_Y) are 32 bytes, hex. identityId is the normalized identity id string, UTF-8 encoded into the slot info.",
  "cases": [
    {
